  "verbalization": "Ardeparin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Pulmonary Embolism (disease) through a chain of indications that link it to Purpura Fulminans, a condition associated with thromboembolic complications. This relationship is supported by the shared indication of Purpura Fulminans with Enoxaparin and Adomiparin, both of which are known to inhibit clot formation and are used in the management of thromboembolic disorders. The presence of Heparin, Bovine, as an indication for Pulmonary Embolism further underscores the role of anticoagulant agents in the development of this disease. The integrated evidence suggests that Ardeparin may exert antithrombotic effects through a mechanism similar to its analogs, potentially contributing to the prevention of thromboembolic events. The strong alignment in the scores across the three paths indicates a robust, though indirect, relationship between Ardeparin and Pulmonary Embolism, mediated through the indication of Purpura Fulminans and its associated anticoagulant agents.",
